// A `#[derive(Row)]` field whose type is **module-qualified**, which is the one shape that puts a
// type name into generated text: a flat `at: time.Instant` is converted by `to_instant(..)` and
// names no type at all, but `Option<time.Instant>` writes the type out twice.
//
// The bridge's first version stripped the module qualifier when reifying a field's type, so this
// generated `Option<Instant>` -- a name that does not resolve in the user's file. Every existing
// fixture passed, because none of them had a qualified type inside an `Option`. The generator is
// handed the name as the source spells it now, and strips it only to look `Instant` up in the
// short-converter table.
use time
use db

#[derive(Row)]
struct Ev {
    at: time.Instant
    maybe: Option<time.Instant>
}

fn main() {
    print("ok")
}
